  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://iatipublisher-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/document-link/92/BSP%20Narrative%20Report-Year%2011787846670.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENABLING ENVIRONMENT SUPPORT</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Work Package 1 focused on strengthening Ghana&apos;s policy and regulatory environment for the
vegetable seed sector while building the knowledge base and communication channels needed
to sustain engagement between Dutch and Ghanaian private-sector actors. During Year 1,
Wageningen University &amp; Research (WUR) and SeedNL engaged closely with key stakeholders,
including the Technical Working Group on Seeds under the Agricultural Working Group, to
translate the findings of the Ghana Seed Sector Assessment into actionable recommendations.
WUR also collaborated with a team from the West Africa Horticulture Innovation Hub at the
University of Ghana to gather input from a broad range of stakeholders. This engagement
informed a National Vegetable Roadmap light. This Road Map Light, which outlines priority
pathways for improving the regulatory and institutional environment for vegetable seeds was
validated in May 2026. At EKN&apos;s request, WUR subsequently expanded the document into a full
National Horticulture Seed Roadmap, scheduled for formal presentation to the Ministry of Food
and Agriculture in September 2026.</narrative>
   </description>
